(6815202, 1024119, 143062, '<td valign="top">Thank You for voting and commenting on this pic.<br/>More info on Johann Georg Elser, the man who attempted to assasinate Hitler, can be found here: <a href="//de.images.search.yahoo.com/search/images?_adv_prop=image&amp;fr=chr-devicevm&amp;va=georg+elser+wilhelmstrasse" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//de.images.search.yahoo.com/search/images?_adv_prop=image&amp;fr=chr-devicevm&amp;va=georg+elser+wilhelmstrasse</a> <br/> <br/>Some pics above will show the sculpture that was used in the pic.  The structure is illuminated from the inside via neon tubes.  <br/> <br/>The technique was simply:  Camera was set to 5 secs, f 7.1 at ISO 200.  During exposure the camera was moved over the 5 seconds from the right to the lower left in a wobbling fashion, sort of in a sinus wave.  In the last fraction of the time before the shutter closed, the camera was held still to achieve a longer imprint of the sculpture.<br/> <br/>I liked how the motion created a 3D effect of the face towards the left.<br/>Minimal post processing followed in digital darkroom. I think it was mostly around increasing the saturation.<br/> <br/>I took this pic while I was in Berlin on my Europe vacation.</td>', 'Thank You for voting and commenting on this pic.More info on Johann Georg Elser, the man who attempted to assasinate Hitler, can be found here: //de.images.search.yahoo.com/search/images?_adv_prop=image&fr=chr-devicevm&va=georg+elser+wilhelmstrasse  Some pics above will show the sculpture that was used in the pic.  The structure is illuminated from the inside via neon tubes.   The technique was simply:  Camera was set to 5 secs, f 7.1 at ISO 200.  During exposure the camera was moved over the 5 seconds from the right to the lower left in a wobbling fashion, sort of in a sinus wave.  In the last fraction of the time before the shutter closed, the camera was held still to achieve a longer imprint of the sculpture. I liked how the motion created a 3D effect of the face towards the left.Minimal post processing followed in digital darkroom. I think it was mostly around increasing the saturation. I took this pic while I was in Berlin on my Europe vacation.', '2012-07-11 04:26:54.000000', NULL, 0),
